platforms-keep-application-components-in-terms-of-widget-scope-semantic = Keep application components in terms of Widget, Scope, semantic events, and typed styles. Put DOM lookup, HTML generation, window creation, and event loops in small host-specific entry points.
platforms-write-the-shared-component-once = Write the shared component once
platforms-this-component-contains-no-web-sys-html-document-or = This component contains no web-sys, HTML document, or window types. Its Cage and event handler have the same ownership and update behavior wherever the widget is mounted.
platforms-forward-only-the-features-you-use = Forward only the features you use
platforms-glory-has-no-default-host-application-features-forward-to = Glory has no default host. Application features forward to facade features, keeping server, browser, and native dependency graphs explicit. web and ssr each select html; hydrate selects web; stream selects ssr and resources; blitz is native-only. For a progressive browser client, stream-web selects stream and hydrate (and therefore web); hydrate the application after the final End frame.
platforms-choose-the-host-entry-point = Choose the host entry point
platforms-launch-requires-an-empty-unclaimed-browser-mount-hydrate-expects = launch requires an empty, unclaimed browser mount. hydrate expects Glory's versioned SSR markers and validates the entire initial subtree before adopting it. The server has no browser input loop; interactivity begins with the browser host.
platforms-windowapp-owns-the-shared-app-and-native-document-shell = WindowApp owns the shared App and native document. Shell owns the desktop event loop and windows. Enable blitz-shell for this entry point; blitz-accesskit additionally enables the optional desktop accessibility bridge.
